-- Row il-72. THE REFERENCES, as typed values: two items, I1 (section 27(c) of the Law) and I2 (section 27(a) of the Law), the provisions they name, the two instructions that repeal sections of the ordinances they name, the footnotes of the pages, and the page facts of the Interpretation Law.
-- Tests of the controls are in an72-tests-controls.l4, tests that pin the readings are in an72-tests-readings.l4, and the assertions that FAIL on purpose (two, one per item) are in an72-tests-red.l4.
--
-- THE QUOTATION LINES.
-- `src:N` lines are expanded mechanically from the excerpt of the Hebrew Wikisource consolidation (UNOFFICIAL, so CONSOLIDATION-ONLY) by tools/srcquote.py; N is the line number in the whole page, which the excerpt's header lists.
-- `ext:[tag]` lines quote the Hebrew read from a deposited page image (registers/source-bundle/pages/); the tag names the deposit: shNNN-pPPP is Sefer HaChukim (SH) issue NNN, printed page PPP; pg1250s1-pN is page N of Supplement no. 1 to Palestine Gazette no. 1250. They are official instruments.
-- `tr:[tag] | LATIN` lines give the Latin form of words quoted on the lines above, and tools/translit.py checks them against the Hebrew and against the string literals below.
-- The Hebrew on the ext lines was copied from the deposited crops, which were viewed after they were cut; the text layers of these old pages are in reversed letter order, so they were used only as a bag of letters (NOTES.md section 3 says which lines could be compared). Every footnote number a page prints after a word is left out of the quoted line.
-- Nothing is quoted from memory. Every date, number and section below is on a quotation line or in NOTES.md. A date typed below is the date the footer of the issue prints, and it is never a day of effect.
-- Letters: "and-" is the prefix vav with maqaf; (d) is the letter dalet in brackets.

§ `References`

